---

<Base
  title="Card"
  description="Card is not a component: Guide to composing semantic cards with Box, Tile, and content components."
>
  <h1>Card</h1>
  <p class="lede">
    Card is a <strong>composition result</strong>, not a system component. The content
    decides its structure; the interaction decides whether the surface is born from
    <a href="/en/components/box">Box</a> or <a href="/en/components/tile">Tile</a>.
  </p>

  <div class="sk-alert" data-tone="info" data-presentation="accent">
    <div class="sk-alert__content">
      <div class="sk-alert__description">
        No existen <code>sk-card</code>, <code>@skryensya/react/card</code> ni
        <code>components/card.css</code>. Importa las piezas que la card realmente usa.
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <h2>Choose by behavior</h2>
  <p>
    "Card" describes the visual form, but does not say what it does. Start with semantics and interaction;
    then compose the content with Stack, Inline, Heading, Text, Badge, Stat or other pieces.
  </p>
  <div class="sk-table-scroll">
    <table class="sk-table">
      <thead>
        <tr><th>The surface…</th><th>Use</th><th>Elemento real</th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>presents content or contains several controls</td><td><a href="/en/components/box">Box</a></td><td><code>article</code>, <code>section</code> o <code>div</code></td></tr>
        <tr><td>complete navigation to a destination</td><td><a href="/en/components/link">TileLink</a></td><td><code>a[href]</code></td></tr>
        <tr><td>execute an action</td><td><a href="/en/components/button">TileButton</a></td><td><code>button</code></td></tr>
        <tr><td>activate a separate option</td><td><a href="/en/components/checkbox">TileCheckbox</a></td><td><code>input[type=checkbox]</code></td></tr>
        <tr><td>choose an exclusive option</td><td><a href="/en/components/radio-group">TileRadioGroup</a></td><td><code>input[type=radio]</code></td></tr>
        <tr><td>reveals content</td><td><a href="/en/components/accordion">Accordion</a></td><td><code>button</code> o <code>details</code></td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
  <p>
    Box and Tile start here from the same surface, subtle edge, radius and <code>lg</code> padding.
    Tile preserves that content and adds the <code>sk-interactive</code> state layer; the difference
    visible appears on hover, focus or press, not on a second card recipe.
  </p>

  <h2>Content card</h2>
  <p>
    Read-only information: Box owns the surface and <code>article</code> preserves the semantics.
    Badge, Heading and Text build the hierarchy without inventing an API Card.
  </p>
  <Showcase
    html={contentHtml}
    react={contentReact}
    label="Content card"
    note="Box + Stack + Badge + Heading + Text"
  />

  <h2 id="noticia">news card</h2>
  <p>
    The entire news leads to a single destination, so it is a TileLink. The title names the link;
    There is no CSS stretched link or card with <code>onClick</code> hidden.
  </p>
  <Showcase
    html={newsHtml}
    react={newsReact}
    label="news card"
    note="TileLink + Text + Icon"
  />

  <h2 id="producto">Product card</h2>
  <p>
    This card has two independent decisions—query and add—which is why it uses Box. Convert all
    the linked surface would nest a button inside a link and produce invalid HTML.
  </p>
  <Showcase
    html={productHtml}
    react={productReact}
    label="Product card"
    note="Box + Badge + Heading + Link + Button"
  />

  <h2 id="enlace">Link card</h2>
  <p>
    A navigation shortcut with a single exit is also TileLink: icon in a sunken well, title
    that names the link, chevron that marks direction. The entire surface retains the link focus;
    there is no second <code>&lt;a&gt;</code> inside nor a <code>onClick</code> in a
    <code>div</code>.
  </p>
  <Showcase
    html={linkHtml}
    react={linkReact}
    label="Link card"
    note="Grid + TileLink + Inline + Icon"
  />

  <h2 id="image">Card with image</h2>
  <p>
    The image is card anatomy, not a new API: <a href="/en/components/image-frame"
    >ImageFrame</a> with <code>data-radius="none"</code> goes flush against the edge and surface
    that contains it already trims (<code>overflow: hidden</code>), so it inherits the radius. The
    <strong>reading</strong> —content or navigation— still chooses the root, the same as without an image:
    Box when read only, TileLink when the entire surface leads to a destination.
  </p>
  <Showcase
    html={mediaHtml}
    react={mediaReact}
    label="Card with image"
    note="Box + ImageFrame + Badge + Heading + Text"
  />
  <p>
    The same card, now interactive: the entire surface navigates, so it is a TileLink with
    <code>data-padding="none"</code> for the image to reach the edge and a body class that
    resets the inset of the text. The title names the link; there is no <code>onClick</code> in a
    <code>div</code> or link stretched by CSS.
  </p>
  <Showcase
    html={mediaLinkHtml}
    react={mediaLinkReact}
    label="Card with image interactiva"
    note="TileLink + ImageFrame + Text + Icon"
  />

  <h2>Action and selection cards</h2>
  <p>
    The geometry may match, but the platform does not: an action is a button and a preference is a
    checkbox. Tile unifies the surface without erasing that difference.
  </p>
  <Showcase
    html={actionSelectionHtml}
    react={actionSelectionReact}
    label="Action and selection"
    note="TileButton + TileCheckbox"
  />

  <h2 id="stat-card">Stat Card</h2>
  <p>
    Stat provides the metric; Box provides the card. The collection uses Grid and fits a column without
    convert Stat to a surface or add a <code>card</code> variant to your API.
  </p>
  <Showcase
    html={statHtml}
    react={statReact}
    label="Business Summary"
    note="Grid + Box + Stat + Icon"
  />

  <h2>Do y do not</h2>
  <div class="sk-grid" data-columns="2" data-gap="md" data-multicol>
    <section class="sk-box" data-surface="surface" data-border="subtle" data-padding="lg">
      <div class="sk-stack" data-gap="sm">
        <span class="sk-badge" data-tone="success">Do · Haz</span>
        <h3 class="sk-heading" data-size="h4">Let the behavior choose the root</h3>
        <ul>
          <li>Use Box for content and for various independent controls.</li>
          <li>Use a semantic Tile when the entire surface has a single intent.</li>
          <li>Preserves headings, lists, prices and statuses as content components.</li>
          <li>Make the visible focus reach the entire interactive surface.</li>
          <li>Let the content determine the height; groups only comparable cards.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </section>
    <section class="sk-box" data-surface="surface" data-border="subtle" data-padding="lg">
      <div class="sk-stack" data-gap="sm">
        <span class="sk-badge" data-tone="danger">Do not Avoid</span>
        <h3 class="sk-heading" data-size="h4">Do not turn appearance into an API</h3>
        <ul>
          <li>Do not create a Card component with <code>news</code>, <code>product</code>, or <code>stat</code> variants.</li>
          <li>Do not put <code>onClick</code> or <code>tabindex</code> in a Box or <code>div</code>.</li>
          <li>Do not nest buttons, links or inputs inside TileLink or TileButton.</li>
          <li>Do not duplicate the same destination on the surface and on an interior link.</li>
          <li>Do not cut important content just to match heights.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>

  <h2>Implementation</h2>
  <p>
    There is no Card import. Import Box or the chosen semantic Tile, its styles and only the
    pieces of content present. This keeps every dependency and every contract visible on the call site.
  </p>
</Base>
